# oracle are the old Rocq oracle's (moss_m2, removed when moss-ref replaced
# it), so they are historical; the suite checks the current verdicts.
# AssumesComplete (AUDIT-CHANGES #57; D20; criteria section 6, fidelity).
# Each assumed item's requirements are in force and its own needs provided.
# Here: f requires T (its signature does not mention it); g assumes f without T and calls it.
# Audit before: accepts. Audit now: rejects (argued from the rules, not run).
# Oracle (moss_m2): rejects ("assuming `f` needs `T` in force (D20)").
# Native (ob-family moss, seed 1h1710x0): rejects ("not available in the current context: `T`").
type T;
assume T { fn f(); }
assume f { fn g() { f(); } }
fn main() {}
